      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the labeled maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. The risks include GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day)\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
