       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and it carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis. Confirming the dose doesn't change that risk for the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a dose within the usual range.** For example, metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any dose you choose up to that limit.\n- **Add a note to the order.** I can flag it for titration review, for example \"uptitrate per pharmacy/attending.\"\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, the safer route is to discuss it with pharmacy or your attending. They can enter or co-sign the order through their own verification process. I can still enter an order within the usual range now, so the patient isn't left without therapy while that happens.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of the in-range options?"
